FreeOIModule -- the class of all free OI-modules over a polynomial OI-algebra
*****************************************************************************

Description
===========

This type implements free OI-modules over polynomial OI-algebras. To make a
FreeOIModule object, use *note makeFreeOIModule: makeFreeOIModule,. To get the
basis elements and rank of a free OI-module, use *note getBasisElements:
getBasisElements, and *note getRank: getRank, respectively. To install the
generators of a component of a free OI-module in a specified width, use *note
installGeneratorsInWidth: installGeneratorsInWidth,.

Each FreeOIModule object comes equipped with either the *note Lex:
(Macaulay2Doc)Lex, monomial order induced by the monomial order on its
underlying polynomial OI-algebra, or the Schreyer monomial order induced by
another free OI-module; see *note makeFreeOIModule: makeFreeOIModule, and *note
OIMonomialOrder: OIMonomialOrder,.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = makePolynomialOIAlgebra(2, x, QQ);       |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = makeFreeOIModule(e, {1,2}, P)            |
|                                                  |
|o2 = Basis symbol: e                              |
|     Basis element widths: {1, 2}                 |
|     Degree shifts: {0, 0}                        |
|     Polynomial OI-algebra: (2, x, QQ, RowUpColUp)|
|     Monomial order: Lex                          |
|                                                  |
|o2 : FreeOIModule                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Functions and methods returning an object of class FreeOIModule:
================================================================

  * *note getFreeOIModule: getFreeOIModule, -- get the free OI-module of an
    element
  * *note makeFreeOIModule: makeFreeOIModule, -- make a FreeOIModule object

