makeFreeOIModule -- make a FreeOIModule object
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeFreeOIModule(e,L,P)
  * Inputs:
      * e, a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * P, an instance of the type *note PolynomialOIAlgebra:
        PolynomialOIAlgebra,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeShifts => ..., default value null
      * OIMonomialOrder => ..., default value Lex
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note FreeOIModule: FreeOIModule,, 

Description
===========

Makes a free OI-module of the form $\bigoplus_{i=1}^s\mathbf{F}^{\text{OI},
d_i}$ over the *note PolynomialOIAlgebra: PolynomialOIAlgebra, object P with
$L=\{d_1,\ldots,d_s\}$ and basis symbol e.

The *note DegreeShifts: DegreeShifts, option is used to specify a shift of
grading. This option must be set to either null for no shifts, or a list of
integers describing the desired shifts.

The *note OIMonomialOrder: OIMonomialOrder, option must be set to either *note
Lex: (Macaulay2Doc)Lex,, for the lexicographic order, or a list of elements of
some free OI-module for the Schreyer order. See below for examples.

Example 1: Lex
==============

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = makePolynomialOIAlgebra(2, x, QQ);                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = makeFreeOIModule(e, {1,1,2}, P, DegreeShifts => {3,2,1})|
|                                                                 |
|o2 = Basis symbol: e                                             |
|     Basis element widths: {1, 1, 2}                             |
|     Degree shifts: {3, 2, 1}                                    |
|     Polynomial OI-algebra: (2, x, QQ, RowUpColUp)               |
|     Monomial order: Lex                                         |
|                                                                 |
|o2 : FreeOIModule                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

Example 2: Schreyer
===================

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = makeFreeOIModule(e, {1,1}, P);                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : installGeneratorsInWidth(F, 2);                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : b = x_(1,1)*e_(2,{1},1)+x_(2,1)*e_(2,{1},2);                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : G = makeFreeOIModule(d, {2}, P, DegreeShifts => {-degree b},            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Basis symbol: d                                                         |
|     Basis element widths: {2}                                               |
|     Degree shifts: {-1}                                                     |
|     Polynomial OI-algebra: (2, x, QQ, RowUpColUp)                           |
|     Monomial order: Schreyer                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : FreeOIModule                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|OIMonomialOrder => {b})                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use makeFreeOIModule:
=============================

  * "makeFreeOIModule(Symbol,List,PolynomialOIAlgebra)"

For the programmer
==================

