OIMonomialOrder -- monomial order option for free OI-modules
************************************************************

Description
===========

Used as an optional argument in *note makeFreeOIModule: makeFreeOIModule, to
specify the desired monomial order.

Permissible values:

  * OIMonomialOrder => "Lex" for the lexicographic order induced by the
    monomial order of the underlying polynomial OI-algebra; see [1, Example
    3.2]
  * OIMonomialOrder => "List" for the Schreyer order induced by a list of
    elements of a free OI-module; see [1, Definition 4.2]

References:

[1] M. Morrow and U. Nagel, Computing Gröbner Bases and Free Resolutions of
OI-Modules, Preprint, arXiv:2303.06725, 2023.

