oiGB -- compute a Gröbner basis for a submodule of a free OI-module
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        oiGB L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value Minimize
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Given a list of elements L belonging to a free OI-module $\mathbf{F}$, this
method computes a Gröbner basis for the submodule generated by L with respect
to the monomial order of $\mathbf{F}$. The *note Verbose:
(Macaulay2Doc)Verbose, option must be either true or false, depending on
whether one wants debug information printed.

The *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Strategy, option has the following
permissible values:

  * Strategy => "FastNonminimal" for no post-processing of the basis
  * Strategy => "Minimize" to minimize the basis after it is computed; see
    *note minimizeOIGB: minimizeOIGB,
  * Strategy => "Reduce" to reduce the basis after it is computed; see *note
    reduceOIGB: reduceOIGB,
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
