oiSyz -- compute a Gröbner basis for the syzygy module of a submodule of a free OI-module
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        oiSyz(G, d)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * d, a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value Minimize
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Given a non-empty Gröbner basis G for a submodule $\mathbf{M}$ of a free
OI-module $\mathbf{F}$, this method computes a Gröbner basis $G'$ for the
syzygy module of $\mathbf{M}$ with respect to the Schreyer order induced by
$G$; see *note OIMonomialOrder: OIMonomialOrder,.

The new Gröbner basis $G'$ lives in an appropriate free OI-module $\mathbf{G}$
with basis symbol d whose basis elements are mapped onto the elements of $G$ by
a canonical surjective map $\varphi:\mathbf{G}\to\mathbf{M}$ (see Definition
4.1 of [1]). Moreover, the degrees of the basis elements of $\mathbf{G}$ are
automatically shifted to coincide with the degrees of the elements of $G$, so
that $\varphi$ is homogeneous if $G$ consists of homogeneous elements. If $G'$
is not empty, then one obtains $\mathbf{G}$ by applying *note getFreeOIModule:
getFreeOIModule, to any element of $G'$. One obtains $\varphi$ by using *note
getSchreyerMap: getSchreyerMap,.

The *note Verbose: (Macaulay2Doc)Verbose, option must be either true or false,
depending on whether one wants debug information printed.

The *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Strategy, option has the following
permissible values:

  * Strategy => "FastNonminimal" for no post-processing of the basis
  * Strategy => "Minimize" to minimize the basis after it is computed; see
    *note minimizeOIGB: minimizeOIGB,
  * Strategy => "Reduce" to reduce the basis after it is computed; see *note
    reduceOIGB: reduceOIGB,
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = makePolynomialOIAlgebra(2, x, QQ);                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = makeFreeOIModule(e, {1,1}, P);                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : installGeneratorsInWidth(F, 2);                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : b = x_(1,2)*x_(1,1)*e_(2,{2},1)+x_(2,2)*x_(2,1)*e_(2,{1},2);            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = oiGB {b}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {x   x   e        + x   x   e       , x   x   x   e        -            |
|       1,2 1,1 2,{2},1    2,2 2,1 2,{1},2   2,3 2,2 1,1 3,{2},2              |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x   x   x   e       }                                                   |
|      2,3 2,1 1,2 3,{1},2                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : oiSyz(G, d)                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {x   d              - x   d             , x   d              -          |
|       2,4 4,{1, 2, 3},2    2,3 4,{1, 2, 4},2   1,2 4,{1, 3, 4},2            |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x   d              - x   d             , x   d           - x   d        |
|      1,1 4,{2, 3, 4},2    1,3 4,{1, 2, 4},2   1,2 3,{1, 3},1    1,1 3,{2,   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|          + 1d             }                                                 |
|     3},1     3,{1, 2, 3},2                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

References:

[1] M. Morrow and U. Nagel, Computing Gröbner Bases and Free Resolutions of
OI-Modules, Preprint, arXiv:2303.06725, 2023.

