oiRes -- compute an OI-resolution
*********************************

  * Usage: 
        oiRes(L, n)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value Minimize
      * TopNonminimal => ..., default value false
      * Verbose => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note OIResolution: OIResolution,, 

Description
===========

Computes an OI-resolution of the submodule generated by L out to homological
degree n. If L consists of homogeneous elements, then the resulting resolution
will be graded and minimal out to homological degree $n-1$. The *note Verbose:
(Macaulay2Doc)Verbose, option must be either true or false, depending on
whether one wants debug information printed.

The *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Strategy, option has the following
permissible values:

  * Strategy => "FastNonminimal" for no post-processing of the Gröbner basis
    computed at each step
  * Strategy => "Minimize" to minimize the Gröbner basis after it is computed
    at each step; see *note minimizeOIGB: minimizeOIGB,
  * Strategy => "Reduce" to reduce the Gröbner basis after it is computed at
    each step; see *note reduceOIGB: reduceOIGB,

The *note TopNonminimal: TopNonminimal, option must be either true or false,
depending on whether one wants the Gröbner basis in homological degree $n-1$ to
be minimized. Therefore, use TopNonminimal => true for no minimization of the
basis in degree $n-1$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = makePolynomialOIAlgebra(2, x, QQ);                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = makeFreeOIModule(e, {1,1}, P);                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : installGeneratorsInWidth(F, 2);                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : b = x_(1,2)*x_(1,1)*e_(2,{2},1)+x_(2,2)*x_(2,1)*e_(2,{1},2);|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : time oiRes({b}, 2, TopNonminimal => true)                   |
| -- used 0.587741s (cpu); 0.428162s (thread); 0s (gc)            |
|                                                                 |
|o5 = 0: (e0, {2}, {-2})                                          |
|     1: (e1, {4}, {-4})                                          |
|     2: (e2, {4, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5}, {-4, -5, -5, -5, -5, -5})       |
|                                                                 |
|o5 : OIResolution                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

